{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"select-tedious-bison","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Observed while fixing a3f5-5c19-faad-417b (2026-08-22): on a clean origin/main checkout (8481a057b69, and reconfirmed with no local diff) on a macOS dev host, tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py::test_five_environment_matrix_has_identical_results_without_gh fails for all 5 params (local/github/jenkins/gitlab/bare vendor envs) while 6 other tests in the file pass and CI's Verified gate is green on the same tree.\n\nThe test asserts identical results across vendor environments WITHOUT gh; a plausible mechanism is host ambient state (gh installed/authenticated, or other env leakage) reaching the supposedly held-out environment matrix — i.e., the test's isolation is incomplete on hosts with gh present. Not reproduced under CI.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Root cause of the host-vs-CI divergence confirmed per /rebar-debug (hypothesis: ambient gh/env leaking through the vendor-env matrix isolation).\n- [ ] Test passes on a host WITH gh installed and authenticated — proven by `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py -q` locally.\n- [ ] No weakening of the held-out contract (the matrix must still prove gh-independence).\n\n## Testing\nReproduce: run `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py::test_five_environment_matrix_has_identical_results_without_gh -q` on a dev host with gh on PATH.","id":"3eb6-6e65-539a-4be1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"bridge provider heldout matrix test fails on dev host (passes in CI)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787448787741111001,"uuid":"19ab7b64-9204-488e-9fdf-6d6980cb799e"}